The {{nihongo|'''Tozai Line'''|東西線|Tōzai-sen}} is a subway line in [[Okami|Okami (大紙)]], [[Okaiken]], operated by [[Okami Metro]]. As its name implies (''Tozai'' means "East-West"), it serves as the primary transverse artery of the Okami Metro network. It connects the eastern coastal port districts of [[Kaimi]], facing the open sea, with the western inland residential suburbs of [[Yonezawa]]. On system maps, the line is color-coded sky blue ({{Okami Metro color|Z}}), and its stations use the prefix "Z".

The Tozai Line is distinctive for its extensive through-service operations with the [[Yonekyu Corporation]], a major private railway. Trains from the eastern terminus at Kaimi travel west across the city, running parallel to the [[Chūō Line (Okami)|Chūō Line]] before continuing past [[Minami-Yonezawa Station|Minami-Yonezawa]] onto the [[Yonekyu Yonezawa Line]].

==History==
Planning for an east-west route began in the post-war reconstruction period to relieve congestion on the [[Sanese National Railways|OR]] [[Chuo Line (OR)|Chuo Line]]. The first segment between the coastal hub of [[Kaimi Station|Kaimi]] and the central district of [[Honmachi-Sanjō Station|Honmachi-Sanjō]] opened on November 1, 1961.

The line was extended westward inland in phases throughout the 1970s. The final underground segment to [[Minami-Yonezawa Station|Minami-Yonezawa]] was completed in 1982. On the same day, reciprocal through-service with the [[Yonekyu Corporation|Yonekyu]] Yonezawa Line commenced, marking the first metro-private rail through-service in the capital.

==Station List==
* All stations are located in [[Okami|Okami City (大紙市)]].
* '''L''': Local (普通) - Stops at all stations.
* '''R''': Rapid (快速) - Skips minor stations to compete with parallel surface lines.
* '''LE''': Limited Express (特急) - "Ocean Liner" through-service to Yonezawa-Onsen.
* Stops: {{small|●}} = Stops, {{small|｜}} = Passes, {{small|▲}} = Alight only (Westbound) / Board only (Eastbound).

